{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection","id":1544867,"title":"Wraiths and Resurrection","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-27T13:31:04-07:00","id":1544867,"title":"Wraiths and Resurrection","content":"So... My Mage wants to resurrect a Wraith.<br /> <br /> I would like to discuss the possibilities of that here.<br /> <br /> 1.) First off, if the Wraith still has its mortal body:<br /> <br /> Well, a dead body is Matter. Thus, to make it live again, you would need Matter 5 and Life 5.<br /> <br /> That grants you the living husk for the deceased to get back into.<br /> <br /> Since this is his own body, although deceased, there should still be a connection, right?<br /> <br /> Next up, it's necessary to tie up the Wraith into the body.<br /> <br /> Usually, creating a human from nothing requires Life 5, Mind 5 and Spirit 5. That is, you create a body, a mind and a soul, and fuse it all together.<br /> <br /> The Wraith already has a mind of his own thou, so would you just need Spirit 5 then?<br /> <br /> 2.) Second, the Wraiths body is no more.<br /> <br /> In that case, you need Prime 2 Life 5 to create a new body. That's easier than Matter 5 Life 5 thou... So... Yeah.<br /> <br /> That's however NOT the &quot;real&quot; body of the Wraith. What would be the implications?<br /> <br /> Regardless of that, it should still be theoretically possible, using Spirit 5 you'll still fuse the &quot;soul&quot; into the body regardless. Maybe the new &quot;reborn&quot; will feel &quot;discomfort&quot; or something else from such a procedure, but it should be possible.<br /> <br /> The consideration about the need or not of Mind 5 remains here.<br /> <br /> Wraiths however appear to be... Incomplete &quot;souls&quot;. They have no Avatars for instance. So, that &quot;reborn&quot; would possibly not be a &quot;full&quot; person?<br /> <br /> Spirit 5 SHOULD be able to recreate the &quot;missing pieces&quot; of the soul thou - it is able to create new Avatars after all, but assuming the Mage doesn't do that, would this new &quot;reborn&quot; keep some of its Arcanoi? What else would they have?<br /> <br /> Would such a &quot;reborn&quot; simply be a Mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T14:21:24-07:00","id":1544869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection#post1544867\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So... My Mage wants to resurrect a Wraith.<br /> <br /> I would like to discuss the possibilities of that here.<br /> <br /> 1.) First off, if the Wraith still has its mortal body:<br /> <br /> Well, a dead body is Matter. Thus, to make it live again, you would need Matter 5 and Life 5.<br /> <br /> That grants you the living husk for the deceased to get back into.<br /> <br /> Since this is his own body, although deceased, there should still be a connection, right?<br /> <br /> Next up, it's necessary to tie up the Wraith into the body.<br /> <br /> Usually, creating a human from nothing requires Life 5, Mind 5 and Spirit 5. That is, you create a body, a mind and a soul, and fuse it all together.<br /> <br /> The Wraith already has a mind of his own thou, so would you just need Spirit 5 then?</div> </div> </div> </div>We could assume that you need Life 5 and Spirit 5 to bind something to a body of another. That would be correct<br /> Matter on the other hand should be 2. Transforming matter to life is Matter 2.<br /> <br /> Yes i think Mind is optional here.<br /> The only thing i can think of is that the recreated body has no mind so when you merge the wraith with the body he still will have no mind. Even his wraith mind as he would be a wraith no more. Just speculating though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/curseborne/1544683-lineage-spell-list?p=1544868#post1544868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2.) Second, the Wraiths body is no more.<br /> <br /> In that case, you need Prime 2 Life 5 to create a new body. That's easier than Matter 5 Life 5 thou... So... Yeah.<br /> <br /> That's however NOT the &quot;real&quot; body of the Wraith. What would be the implications?<br /> <br /> Regardless of that, it should still be theoretically possible, using Spirit 5 you'll still fuse the &quot;soul&quot; into the body regardless. Maybe the new &quot;reborn&quot; will feel &quot;discomfort&quot; or something else from such a procedure, but it should be possible.<br /> <br /> The consideration about the need or not of Mind 5 remains here.<br /> <br /> Wraiths however appear to be... Incomplete &quot;souls&quot;. They have no Avatars for instance. So, that &quot;reborn&quot; would possibly not be a &quot;full&quot; person?<br /> <br /> Spirit 5 SHOULD be able to recreate the &quot;missing pieces&quot; of the soul thou - it is able to create new Avatars after all, but assuming the Mage doesn't do that, would this new &quot;reborn&quot; keep some of its Arcanoi? What else would they have?<br /> <br /> Would such a &quot;reborn&quot; simply be a Mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this still would create a full person. With Life 5 and Spirit 5 you should be capable of creating a perfect fit body for the wraith. As for the avatar i would assume its the ST decision if this would alow to retain the avatar or lose it and never be able to awaken.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T20:45:01-07:00","id":1544873,"title":"","content":"Converting a corpse to a living body is probably Life 5/Matter 4 as dead bodies are likely complex matter. Spirit 5 should be fine for fusing a wraith with said body. The Mage shouldn\u2019t need to recreate the mind buuuuut\u2026.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a lot of funny business on the wraith end to deal with.<br /> <br /> First, as you say, the wraith isn\u2019t the complete soul, but the complete soul isn\u2019t gone per se. The Shadow and Eidolon are still there so there\u2019s nothing to recreate. But do they want to play along? Neither wants to live again, after all. They might even fight the process and take extra successes.<br /> <br /> Second, there\u2019s an even better case that the wraith isn\u2019t the complete mind. So it really matters if the goal is to bring the wraith to life or bring back the person who died. It\u2019s not necessarily the same effect.<br /> <br /> Third, where is the soul of the wraith and what does it take to bring it to the body? At the very least the mage needs to pull it across the shroud. Again this is not necessarily the same thing as just pulling the wraith to the body. The Eidolon and Avatar may be elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Finally, what if the wraith has lost Corpus or Passions to harrowing? You\u2019ll need to decide if that is actual soul damage to repair or just a loss of grip on the world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T00:01:05-07:00","id":1544875,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1544873#post1544873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Converting a corpse to a living body is probably Life 5/Matter 4 as dead bodies are likely complex matter. Spirit 5 should be fine for fusing a wraith with said body. The Mage shouldn\u2019t need to recreate the mind buuuuut\u2026.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you're right, I believe Matter 4 is the more fitting level here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There\u2019s a lot of funny business on the wraith end to deal with. </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what I was hoping for!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First, as you say, the wraith isn\u2019t the complete soul, but the complete soul isn\u2019t gone per se. The Shadow and Eidolon are still there so there\u2019s nothing to recreate. But do they want to play along? Neither wants to live again, after all. They might even fight the process and take extra successes. </div> </div> </div>The Shadow and the Eidolon probably wouldn't want to, but who cares? The guy is a mad Etherite &quot;scientist&quot;, if you call what he does as &quot;science&quot; rather than things that could break the Geneva convention... In fact, if they resist so much the better! Because his &quot;science&quot; project is to build a full on &quot;living Wraith&quot;.<br /> <br /> The question thou is that the Avatar at least seems to be gone for a walk, since Wraiths cannot awaken. Therefore, that part at least is probably gone to do its own thing.<br /> <br /> But I don't care, if needed be I'll just make a brand new Avatar for my lab rats. But only if necessary and it doesn't interfere with the &quot;living Wraith&quot; status. If making an Avatar just makes the thing turn into a normal human, that would be a massive failure for my super ethical &quot;scientist&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, there\u2019s an even better case that the wraith isn\u2019t the complete mind. So it really matters if the goal is to bring the wraith to life or bring back the person who died. It\u2019s not necessarily the same effect. </div> </div> </div>I don't give 2 cares to the people who died. I want my little living Wraiths pets of my own.<br /> <br /> Sure, I'll also bring some to be fully resurrected, to be turned back into the people they were before. Just for the sake of having a control group, but also for the giggles and for the sake of &quot;science&quot;.<br /> <br /> But the main purpose would be to create true &quot;living Wraiths&quot;, rather than just merely resurrecting them into their former selves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Third, where is the soul of the wraith and what does it take to bring it to the body? At the very least the mage needs to pull it across the shroud. Again this is not necessarily the same thing as just pulling the wraith to the body. The Eidolon and Avatar may be elsewhere. </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Avatar is a problem. For all that matters, Avatars are annoyingly absent in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The Eidolon seem to be inside the Wraith itself thou.<br /> <br /> That's not a problem to me thou, I can just simply create new Avatars for the Reborn if necessary. It would, in fact, be even better! <br /> <br /> Because, you see, if I have the original body and all original parts of the Soul and perhaps even of the mind of the Wraith, then the end result would be... Boring. Boring, as in, not conductive towards further experimentation. Because all pieces would fit, and the Reborn would be well adjust (or at least as well adjust as it could be).<br /> <br /> If however, the end result is a combination of several different pieces, that resulting Frankenstein monsters would be sublime.<br /> <br /> For instance, how will the &quot;soul&quot; adjust to a body to which it never really belonged? What if I force a Wraith that used to be a male into a freshly out of the oven female body, or if I change the race or make any other kinds of modifications (height, weight, appearance), with the more expressive the change the better? Would his soul start to reject the body, or would his mind begin to crumble?<br /> <br /> What if I install a new Avatar to his missing soul, preferably one Avatar that goes directly against the core principles of said Wraith? Would his soul start to fight against itself? And how would that be?<br /> <br /> For the Avatar however, it is possible to live without one. The Techies create clones without Avatars all the time, and victims of Gilgul can still be left alive. My fear is that, if I give the Wraith an Avatar, the Reborn will just simply become a &quot;common&quot; resurrected, aka just a &quot;normal&quot; person (with a weird origin and perhaps some deep internal conflicts), rather than a real &quot;living Wraith&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Shadow, a real Wraith has a Shadow, so I hope it can be tagged along in the ride just as it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, what if the wraith has lost Corpus or Passions to harrowing? You\u2019ll need to decide if that is actual soul damage to repair or just a loss of grip on the world.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Oh, if it's soul damage, so much the better! I can barely wait to study the effects that a &quot;shredded soul&quot; have on a living being!<br /> <br /> My final question: would such a Reborn keep its Arcanoi (since I'm trying as best as I can to keep it as a &quot;living Wraith&quot; rather than just a &quot;regular&quot; resurrection), at least with the same kinds of restrictions as the Risen?<br /> <br /> Would this being be somewhat of a Mummy? I'll also add an &quot;immortality protocol&quot;, upon which this &quot;living Wraith&quot; would self-resurrect every time it is killed, even if its entire body is destroyed (basically turning it into a living wonder with a Prime 2, Life 5, Spirit 5 Mind 5 effect that always recreates its body in case it is destroyed). Or would it be more like a truly &quot;living Risen&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T07:16:51-07:00","id":1544887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1544875#post1544875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shadow and the Eidolon probably wouldn't want to, but who cares? The guy is a mad Etherite &quot;scientist&quot;, if you call what he does as &quot;science&quot; rather than things that could break the Geneva convention... In fact, if they resist so much the better! Because his &quot;science&quot; project is to build a full on &quot;living Wraith&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, a mage could take that attitude, but that's not really my point. I wasn't bringing up moral issues but metaphysical ones. It's not clear exactly what state the soul is in, but its not the same one it was in life. It could be that it is split into multiple parts, which is probably the best case scenario at least in terms of difficulty. More likely, though, the parts are all still connected but not unified in location or motivation. In that case the mage has to figure out how to do that.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not trying to force a certain path here. The mage could choose forced reunification, forcing them all into a body without reunification, or even cutting the wraith part free and and leaving the others to do whatever they do, but all of them are a challenge. Yes, Spirit 5 covers all three of those, but this is still the kind of thing that should require a lot of research. Skill rolls make a lot of sense for something like this, and there should be serious risk of destroying the wraith if the mage rushes things. And the Shadow and Eidolon's resistance will make things more difficult regardless of the path.<br /> <br /> Also, I didn't just bring up the difficulty of bringing the parts to the body to highlight reunification. Moving in and out of the Underworld is indicated to be A Very Hard Thing<sup>TM</sup>. Presumably pulling a wraith out is as well. It will be even harder if the mage doesn't really know where they are or how they are connected. This is one place where Spirit 5 alone might not be enough. Now that's purely optional because I don't think the given examples of resurrection deal with that, but it can be an issue if you want it to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1544875#post1544875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The question thou is that the Avatar at least seems to be gone for a walk, since Wraiths cannot awaken. Therefore, that part at least is probably gone to do its own thing.<br /> <br /> But I don't care, if needed be I'll just make a brand new Avatar for my lab rats. But only if necessary and it doesn't interfere with the &quot;living Wraith&quot; status. If making an Avatar just makes the thing turn into a normal human, that would be a massive failure for my super ethical &quot;scientist&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is largely an ST call, but for my part I would include the Avatar as one of the parts of the soul that needs to be brought back. It's not awakening the wraith, but that doesn't mean it was cut free. Just assuming it is gone and grafting on a new one could leave this newly revived person with two Avatars but one trapped who knows where. This seems like a golden opportunity to unleash strange and dangerous consequences on the reborn wraith, the mage, and the world.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you have to, but I personally couldn't resist. It isn't even a punishment, its just too strange a situation to sweep under the rug.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1544875#post1544875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For instance, how will the &quot;soul&quot; adjust to a body to which it never really belonged? What if I force a Wraith that used to be a male into a freshly out of the oven female body, or if I change the race or make any other kinds of modifications (height, weight, appearance), with the more expressive the change the better? Would his soul start to reject the body, or would his mind begin to crumble?<br /> <br /> What if I install a new Avatar to his missing soul, preferably one Avatar that goes directly against the core principles of said Wraith? Would his soul start to fight against itself? And how would that be?<br /> <br /> For the Avatar however, it is possible to live without one. The Techies create clones without Avatars all the time, and victims of Gilgul can still be left alive. My fear is that, if I give the Wraith an Avatar, the Reborn will just simply become a &quot;common&quot; resurrected, aka just a &quot;normal&quot; person (with a weird origin and perhaps some deep internal conflicts), rather than a real &quot;living Wraith&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the Shadow, a real Wraith has a Shadow, so I hope it can be tagged along in the ride just as it is.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is a table decision. Physical and metaphysical dysmorphia can be as much or as little an issue as will be fun for the table. I'd recommend talking it out in advance.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1544875#post1544875\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, if it's soul damage, so much the better! I can barely wait to study the effects that a &quot;shredded soul&quot; have on a living being!<br /> <br /> My final question: would such a Reborn keep its Arcanoi (since I'm trying as best as I can to keep it as a &quot;living Wraith&quot; rather than just a &quot;regular&quot; resurrection), at least with the same kinds of restrictions as the Risen?<br /> <br /> Would this being be somewhat of a Mummy? I'll also add an &quot;immortality protocol&quot;, upon which this &quot;living Wraith&quot; would self-resurrect every time it is killed, even if its entire body is destroyed (basically turning it into a living wonder with a Prime 2, Life 5, Spirit 5 Mind 5 effect that always recreates its body in case it is destroyed). Or would it be more like a truly &quot;living Risen&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Largely up to you. I wouldn't give it Arcanoi and an awakened Avatar at the same time except as part of the aforementioned second Avatar scenario. <br /> <br /> I would say that since you specified an amoral Etherite and many a pulp sci-fi story has had ill-though resurrection experiments end in tragedy and evil, I'm inclined to look for ways that this could all go horribly wrong. Again, this isn't a punishment so much as playing into themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T07:55:02-07:00","id":1544888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1544887#post1544887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well yes, a mage could take that attitude, but that's not really my point. I wasn't bringing up moral issues but metaphysical ones. It's not clear exactly what state the soul is in, but its not the same one it was in life. It could be that it is split into multiple parts, which is probably the best case scenario at least in terms of difficulty. More likely, though, the parts are all still connected but not unified in location or motivation. In that case the mage has to figure out how to do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm... I wonder if a conjunctional Spirit + Correspondence could be able to locate the... Location (locate the location \ud83d\ude22\ud83e\udd22) of these missing parts.<br /> <br /> Assuming for a short moment that it could... That could be problematic, since it would answer the question &quot;where do Avatars go when they get bored&quot;. But... It opens up many possibilities.<br /> <br /> That however would be Spirit 5 Correspondence 5 quite probably, there's no indication that Avatars are having their parties anywhere on the Tellurian, so probably they are hiding somewhere at the Deep Umbra... Maybe. But that science project just suddenly became even better! So many unanswered question at the tip of my hand, all I need to do is seize them.... Oh, delicious!<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I'm not trying to force a certain path here. The mage could choose forced reunification, forcing them all into a body without reunification, or even cutting the wraith part free and and leaving the others to do whatever they do, but all of them are a challenge. Yes, Spirit 5 covers all three of those, but this is still the kind of thing that should require a lot of research. Skill rolls make a lot of sense for something like this, and there should be serious risk of destroying the wraith if the mage rushes things. And the Shadow and Eidolon's resistance will make things more difficult regardless of the path. </div> </div> </div>Yes, this will be no easy feat, undoubtedly. But that's what makes the reward so much more juicier.<br /> <br /> My only problem with reunification is if that leads to a normal person rather than a freakish wraith that is somehow truly living and breathing. I have a feeling that getting everything on it's proper place would just create a &quot;normal&quot; sleeper, even if the missing parts are done by recreated pieces using Spirit (in that case, it would probably lead towards a dysfunction &quot;normal&quot; person)<br /> <br /> At any rate, I would like to try out the 3 possibilities - true reunification of all the pieces of the soul (and possibly restoring the original body), reintegration of the missing pieces by building them anew, and reborning it without the missing pieces.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I didn't just bring up the difficulty of bringing the parts to the body to highlight reunification. Moving in and out of the Underworld is indicated to be A Very Hard Thing<sup>TM</sup>. Presumably pulling a wraith out is as well. It will be even harder if the mage doesn't really know where they are or how they are connected. This is one place where Spirit 5 alone might not be enough. Now that's purely optional because I don't think the given examples of resurrection deal with that, but it can be an issue if you want it to be. </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThat will be taken into consideration.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is largely an ST call, but for my part I would include the Avatar as one of the parts of the soul that needs to be brought back. It's not awakening the wraith, but that doesn't mean it was cut free. Just assuming it is gone and grafting on a new one could leave this newly revived person with two Avatars but one trapped who knows where. This seems like a golden opportunity to unleash strange and dangerous consequences on the reborn wraith, the mage, and the world.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying you have to, but I personally couldn't resist. It isn't even a punishment, its just too strange a situation to sweep under the rug. </div> </div> </div>But wouldn't that be like someone that suffered Gilgul, or like one of the Techie clones with the &quot;no soul&quot; trait?<br /> <br /> Hmmm... On the other hand thou... In the case of the Wraith, perhaps it is not so... Because the Wraiths Avatar didn't suffer Gilgul, neither was it created without one...<br /> <br /> Hmmm... I like the idea of having 2 Avatars... The more Frankensteinian the better<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Largely up to you. I wouldn't give it Arcanoi and an awakened Avatar at the same time except as part of the aforementioned second Avatar scenario. </div> </div> </div>Oh no, I wouldn't consider this... Thing... As eligible to awakening. Just like werewolves or Changelings or Vampires. It would have its own twisted &quot;soul&quot; that can't awaken, probably.<br /> <br /> But I think Arcanoi are fair game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would say that since you specified an amoral Etherite and many a pulp sci-fi story has had ill-though resurrection experiments end in tragedy and evil, I'm inclined to look for ways that this could all go horribly wrong. Again, this isn't a punishment so much as playing into themes. </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. Any idea of gruesome consequences would be appreciated. Sure, Reborn Spectres would be all fun and game obviously, and even for regular Wraiths I believe the problems that the Risen have would fit well, but besides just Shadow shenanigans, what other gruesome consequences could there be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T13:06:09-07:00","id":1545065,"title":"","content":"As I see it, the idea isn't so much to &quot;resurrect&quot; as to ... put a Wraith in a meat mecha so he can act in the land of the living<br /> <br /> That being the case, I would think Life 5 + Spirit 4 it's enough. I would look at the rules Wraith use for Embody 4/5 to see the results. Probably only big difference it's that Wraith doesn't need to power it, and at the same time isn't free to cancel it. Perhaps there's something else, tho, I'm not a Wraith expert","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-01T07:02:19-07:00","id":1545132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544867-wraiths-and-resurrection?p=1545065#post1545065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I see it, the idea isn't so much to &quot;resurrect&quot; as to ... put a Wraith in a meat mecha so he can act in the land of the living<br /> <br /> That being the case, I would think Life 5 + Spirit 4 it's enough. I would look at the rules Wraith use for Embody 4/5 to see the results. Probably only big difference it's that Wraith doesn't need to power it, and at the same time isn't free to cancel it. Perhaps there's something else, tho, I'm not a Wraith expert</div> </div> </div> </div>Not exactly. Yes, what you're suggesting is a &quot;Wraith-Meat-Mecha&quot;.<br /> <br /> That's not what I want. Your suggestion would be akin to a Risen, or to a Wraith using a permanent Embody or permanently puppeteering a body that doesn't rot away.<br /> <br /> What I want however is a living being with a Wraith soul.<br /> <br /> Take Changelings for instance. They have human bodies, they are living beings... But they don't have normal human souls. They have Fae souls &quot;latched&quot; into them like &quot;dimensional parasites&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is also the case for Were-beasts and even vampires too. Oh, it is also the case for Fomori and... Kami? I forgot the name, it's basically the same as Fomori, but they are &quot;infected&quot; by Gaian spirits rather than Wyrm ones.<br /> <br /> In fact, in my mind this would be closer to Mummies than anything else.<br /> <br /> Thus, the idea is to have them being fully and truly alive, but keeping their Wraith souls as they are. Not just simply binding them into a flesh puppet. Hence why it is necessary the full Spirit 5 to truly fuse soul and body, rather than just binding them into the flesh for them to inhabit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}